 "answer": "**Part A**\nBy Fermat's Little Theorem, since 191 is prime, $29^{190} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{191}$. \n$742 = 3 \\times 190 + 172$, so $29^{742} \\equiv 29^{172} \\pmod{191}$.\nComputing successive squares modulo 191:\n- $29^2 = 841 \\equiv 77$\n- $29^4 = 77^2 = 5929 \\equiv 8$\n- $29^8 = 8^2 = 64$\n- $29^{16} = 64^2 = 4096 \\equiv 85$\n- $29^{32} = 85^2 = 7225 \\equiv 158 \\equiv -33$\n- $29^{64} = (-33)^2 = 1089 \\equiv 134 \\equiv -57$\n- $29^{128} = (-57)^2 = 3249 \\equiv 2$\n\nThen $29^{172} = 29^{128} \\times 29^{32} \\times 29^8 \\times 29^4 \\equiv 2 \\times (-33) \\times 64 \\times 8 \\equiv -66 \\times 512 \\equiv -66 \\times 130 = -8580 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{191}$.\n\n**Part B**\nTotal units sold = $97 + 33 + 85 + 104 + 50 + 120 = 489$ units.\nUnder FIFO, the inventory is consumed as follows:\n- Lot 1: 57 units at $\\$13.55 = \\$772.35$\n- Lot 2: 77 units at $\\$13.89 = \\$1,069.53$\n- Lot 3: 80 units at $\\$8.02 = \\$641.60$\n- Lot 4: 159 units at $\\$4.91 = \\$780.69$\n- Lot 5: 80 units at $\\$4.91 = \\$392.80$\n- Lot 6: $489 - (57 + 77 + 80 + 159 + 80) = 36$ units at $\\$8.75 = \\$315.00$\n\nTotal COGS = $772.35 + 1069.53 + 641.60 + 780.69 + 392.80 + 315.00 = \\$3,971.97$.\n\n**Part C**\nTax brackets on $\\$81,900$:\n- 12% on the first $\\$12,500 = \\$1,500.00$\n- 24% on the next $\\$39,500$ $(\\$52,000 - \\$12,500) = \\$9,480.00$\n- 35% on the remaining $\\$29,900$ $(\\$81,900 - \\$52,000) = \\$10,465.00$\nTotal tax before credit = $\\$1,500 + \\$9,480 + \\$10,465 = \\$21,445.00$.\n\nTax credit reduction:\n- Excess income over $\\$50,000 = \\$81,900 - \\$50,000 = \\$31,900$\n- Reduction = $5\\% \\times \\$31,900 = \\$1,595.00$\n- Net credit = $\\$1,800 - \\$1,595 = \\$205.00$\n\nTotal tax owed = $\\$21,445.00 - \\$205.00 = \\$21,240.00$.\n\n**Part D**\nSubtotal for 633 units:\n- First 100 units at $\\$5.00 = \\$500.00$\n- Next 200 units at $\\$4.25 = \\$850.00$\n- Remaining 333 units at $\\$3.50 = \\$1,165.50$\n- Subtotal = $\\$500.00 + \\$850.00 + \\$1,165.50 = \\$2,515.50$\n\nSince $\\$2,515.50 > \\$2,500$, a 3% discount applies:\n- Discounted subtotal = $\\$2,515.50 \\times 0.97 = \\$2,440.035$\n\nAdding 8.0% sales tax:\n- Total = $\\$2,440.035 \\times 1.08 = \\$2,635.2378 \\approx \\$2,635.24$.\n\nFINAL: 15; 3971.97; 21240; 2635.24"
